! Test v1.09.0 (3/4): smeared analytical UKS gradient, RELAXED
! moment.  O2, %mult 1 input (the relaxed-moment grand-canonical
! spin distribution moves the magnetization away from the seed),
! HF/STO-3G, Gaussian sigma = 0.15 Ha.  Exercises the per-spin
! fractional Pulay densities under the SINGLE shared-mu constraint.
! Validated against Richardson-extrapolated central FD of F along
! the bond: |FD_R - g| = 3e-9 Ha/bohr; the fixed-moment twin
! (%smearing_moment fixed) validates to 2.7e-9.  Expected
! (container reference):
!   relaxed:  O1 gZ = -0.16184173,  O2 gZ = 0.16184173
!   fixed:    O1 gZ = -0.15768495,  O2 gZ = 0.15768495
%method  HF
%basis   sto-3g
%job     gradient
%print_grad
%scf_etol 1e-10
%scf_maxiter 300
%mult    1
%spin    unrestricted
%smearing gauss
%smearing_sigma 0.15
%smearing_moment relaxed
*geometry angstrom
 O   0.000000    0.000000    0.000000
 O   0.000000    0.000000    1.300000
*end
